{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1099572-non-fiction-online-resources-for-chronicle-of-darkness","id":1099572,"title":"Non-Fiction Online Resources for Chronicle of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-02T10:45:03-07:00","id":1099572,"title":"Non-Fiction Online Resources for Chronicle of Darkness","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">As I'm sure many of you have noticed, education is kinda a theme with me. I've started to compile some online resources that will apply to each gameline</span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">. Since CofD is set in a dark mirror of our world, there are a lot of materials that could go in this post, but I will try to be selective. While I am keeping Chronicles in mind while I do this, you could use these links for any other RPG that is set on historical Earth (I\u2019m looking at you, Call of Cthulhu!) Some links may show up more than once if they fit in multiple categories.</span></span> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">This post is very much a work in progress and probably will never be complete because of the broad </span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">availability</span></span><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> of applicable materials. If you know of a resource that you don\u2019t see on my list, please feel free to PM or comment to say what the resource is and why it should be included on the list. I\u2019ll do my best to add it in.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">General Websites</span></span></span></span><ul><li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fuser%2Fcrashcourse&amp;t=MGVkNmZlMjM0NDBiYjAyMGNkYmU1MTBlM2IzM2E5MTYzMzJhOGY3Nyx3WXZhbml1cQ%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161295099211%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-eberron&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">Crash Course</a>: It\u2019s free, it\u2019s on Youtube, and it\u2019s in a ten-minute episodic format.</li> <li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.coursera.org&amp;t=YWI3OGM0ZjY5ZTFmMDE0N2YwZDA1YzVmYWQyZTY0NzQ0OWY2NGIzMyx3WXZhbml1cQ%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161295099211%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-eberron&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">Coursera</a>: Coursera is a website where university level classes are available for free. You can also get certifications from Coursera for a fee so you can build your resume while planning your next chronicle.</li> <li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.dancarlin.com%2Fhardcore-history-series%2F&amp;t=OTRiNTk3MDhkYmRlYzJhYTUzMjMwMDU5NDFkYTg3NTJkNmFhNzAzNSx3WXZhbml1cQ%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161295099211%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-eberron&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">Dan Carlin\u2019s Hardcore History</a>: Dan loves historical \u201cWhat if?\u201d moments, and with good reason. If you want to hear the most badass historical stories, examine how drugs, alcohol, and human stupidity impacted history, or get a sense of what it was like to live through the most brutal historical eras, this is the place for you.</li> <li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.edx.org%2F&amp;t=ZWY4MzAyN2YwYTk1NzhmMWZhOTg5MmMwYzIxZWNjMzFlNjMzNjU2MixlNXN5WmVjVA%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161594382696%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-planescape&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">edX</a>: Another excellent site with free courses that you can upgrade for a certificate. A good place to look for courses in the humanities and religion.</li> <li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.thegreatcourses.com%2F&amp;t=OTk2NzhiZDQ0OTMxMmIzMGNkZTNhMWM2ODRlZjUwZGU5MDk4NmNlZix3WXZhbml1cQ%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161295099211%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-eberron&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">Great Course</a>/<a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thegreatcoursesplus.com%2Fhome&amp;t=MjVmNGZjM2ZhNzU3NTc0MTBlNjk1MDNlMTY0ZmQ5MTE5OTdmOTYxZSx3WXZhbml1cQ%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161295099211%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-eberron&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">Great Courses Plus</a>: GC and GC+ are not free services, but they have such an extraordinarily high production value that you can understand why. History, science, culinary theory, economics, anything you can think of is covered in the Great Courses catalogue. Great Courses Plus is their streaming service, which at $15/month for an annual subscription is a killer deal.</li> <li><a href=\"https://books.google.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Google Books</a>/<a href=\"https://scholar.google.ca/\" target=\"_blank\">Google Scholar</a>: My first goto for research of any kind, and the first place I advise my students to begin their research. Seriously, I\u2019ve written papers, then had them published just using these two. Use them.</li> <li><a href=\"https://www.jstor.org/\" target=\"_blank\">JSTOR</a>: If you have operated in any kind of academic circle for the last two and a half decades, you know JSTOR. Full access is tough to come by unless you are currently enrolled in a university, but you can still sign up for free to get access to journals on topics you just can\u2019t find anywhere else (like the Mutapa Empire). Sign up with multiple users if you have to. It works. Trust me.</li> <li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=http%3A%2F%2Foyc.yale.edu%2F&amp;t=MTUyMGE4ODgxZTQzMjIwNGM2OThkN2U4YWZiYmJhYTM0NGU4MzI0YixlNXN5WmVjVA%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161594382696%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-planescape&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">Open Yale Courses</a>: University classes, taped lectures, and course materials, all from one of the best educational institution in the world. Take advantage of them.</li> <li><a href=\"https://vault.fbi.gov/\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault</a>: Declassified FBI documents. A lot more of them involve the paranormal than you may expect. An excellent source of inspiration both for things that actually happened or that people think happened.</li> <li><a href=\"http://writingwithcolor.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Writing with Colour</a>: The best place to go to check yourself for unintentionally problematic depictions of POC in your games. Also a great read if you are looking for details and cultural beats for NPCs you don\u2019t share a background with. They are awesome and you\u2019d be surprised how many chronicle ideas you can get just by binging their archive.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">*************</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Crossover Chronicles</span></span></span></span><ul><li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fuser%2FTheGreatWar&amp;t=Y2VhN2E2MTFiZTgxNTFlNDY5YzVhMmEwMzkzZmY4MzA2YTJkNmI2Nix3WXZhbml1cQ%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161295099211%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-eberron&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">The Great War</a>: Coverage of WW1, on a week by week basis, 100 years later. World War I changed the world, for mortals and supernaturals alike.</li> <li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=https%3A%2F%2Fitunes.apple.com%2Fus%2Fpodcast%2Fthe-history-of-rome%2Fid261654474&amp;t=MTM5OTJkN2FmOTRmOTU3YThlNGJkNGUzMjYyNmUwYmY5N2NhMzU0ZSx3WXZhbml1cQ%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161295099211%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-eberron&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">The History of Rome Podcast</a>: Rome is one of the two cities that broadly unifies all of the Chronicle of Darkness gamelines. This is the best history of Rome you will ever hear, so I suggest using it.</li> <li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.revolutionspodcast.com%2F&amp;t=YTlhNGE1MzU0MDc2NzZmYzQ1MWFjYmMxNmQyN2IzZTI0YzVjNTQzZCx3WXZhbml1cQ%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161295099211%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-eberron&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">Revolutions Podcast</a>: An excellent look at what happens when people get fed up with their governments. A number of the Revolutions covered within have shown up in multiple gamelines.</li> <li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCd4V3I7nYybm4nKwONcOSdA\" target=\"_blank\">Begin Japanology</a>: A Japanese Production specifically targeting Westerners seeking education about what Japan is really like as opposed to the pop culture portrayal. Invaluable for games set in Tokyo. I used to be able to find all of Begin Japanology on Youtube, courtesy of the company that produced them, but now many of them have disappeared. You can find an episode list <a href=\"http://japanology.tv/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</li> <li><a href=\"https://www.thegreatcoursesplus.com/show/understanding_japan_a_cultural_history\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding Japan - A Cultural History</a>: An excellent look at how Japan\u2019s history shaped its evolution into the modern nation that forms that basis of the Tokyo crossover setting.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Dark Eras</span></span></span></span><ul><li><i>Ancient Bloodlines/Mysteries (<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/61617/Ancient-Bloodlines?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>/<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/61284/Ancient-Mysteries?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>)</i><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.thegreatcoursesplus.com/foundations-of-eastern-civilization\" target=\"_blank\">Foundations of Eastern Civilization</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fuser%2FTheGreatWar&amp;t=Y2VhN2E2MTFiZTgxNTFlNDY5YzVhMmEwMzkzZmY4MzA2YTJkNmI2Nix3WXZhbml1cQ%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161295099211%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-eberron&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">The Great War</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.thegreatcoursesplus.com/history-of-the-united-states\" target=\"_blank\">History of the United States 2nd Edition</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.thegreatcoursesplus.com/the-us-and-the-middle-east-1914-to-9-11\" target=\"_blank\">The United States and the Middle East - 1914 to 9/11</a></li> </ul></li> <li><i>Dark Eras (<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/178583/Chronicles-of-Darkness-Dark-Eras?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>)</i><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/learn/aristotle\" target=\"_blank\">Ancient Philosophy - Aristotle &amp; His Successors</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/learn/plato\" target=\"_blank\">Ancient Philosophy - Plato &amp; His Predecessors</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://paris-atlas-historique.fr/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">Atlas Historique de Paris</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCd4V3I7nYybm4nKwONcOSdA\" target=\"_blank\">Begin Japanology</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://youtu.be/SPY-hr-8-M0\" target=\"_blank\">Digital Tour of Tutor London</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.thegreatcoursesplus.com/foundations-of-eastern-civilization\" target=\"_blank\">Foundations of Eastern Civilization</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fuser%2FTheGreatWar&amp;t=Y2VhN2E2MTFiZTgxNTFlNDY5YzVhMmEwMzkzZmY4MzA2YTJkNmI2Nix3WXZhbml1cQ%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161295099211%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-eberron&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">The Great War</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.thegreatcoursesplus.com/history-of-the-united-states\" target=\"_blank\">History of the United States 2nd Edition</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.coursera.org%2Flearn%2Findigenous-canada&amp;t=N2NiMTdiZjIyMzU2YzIyYzY2NzE5OGQ1YTdlMDM2NWEyYmYzZDYyZCx3WXZhbml1cQ%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161295099211%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-eberron&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">Indigenous Canada</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/learn/introancientegypt\" target=\"_blank\">Introduction Ancient Egypt and Its Civilisation</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/learn/magic-middle-ages\" target=\"_blank\">Magic in the Middle Ages</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thegreatcoursesplus.com%2Fmaya-to-aztec-ancient-mesoamerica-revealed&amp;t=MDA3NzYwZjFmY2ZmNWI3ODMzYTM5ODRkZDE1OTc5M2M5NDFmZjA5NCxXSjhSMVpmNw%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161358760096%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-chronicles-of-darkness&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">Maya to Aztec - Ancient Mesoamerica Revealed</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://exploration.urban.free.fr/igc/indexus.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Underground Atlas of Paris</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.thegreatcoursesplus.com/show/understanding_japan_a_cultural_history\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding Japan - A Cultural History</a></li> </ul></li> <li><i>Dark Eras Companion (<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/207879/Chronicles-of-Darkness-Dark-Eras-Companion?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>)</i><ul><li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fuser%2FTheGreatWar&amp;t=Y2VhN2E2MTFiZTgxNTFlNDY5YzVhMmEwMzkzZmY4MzA2YTJkNmI2Nix3WXZhbml1cQ%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161295099211%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-eberron&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">The Great War</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.thegreatcoursesplus.com/history-of-the-united-states\" target=\"_blank\">History of the United States 2nd Edition</a></li> <li><a href=\"http://t.umblr.com/redirect?z=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.coursera.org%2Flearn%2Findigenous-canada&amp;t=N2NiMTdiZjIyMzU2YzIyYzY2NzE5OGQ1YTdlMDM2NWEyYmYzZDYyZCx3WXZhbml1cQ%3D%3D&amp;b=t%3Adpg2Y_ZoazecWjw3yfuk9g&amp;p=http%3A%2F%2Fdailyplanescape.tumblr.com%2Fpost%2F161295099211%2Fnon-fiction-resources-for-eberron&amp;m=0\" target=\"_blank\">Indigenous Canada</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/learn/introancientegypt\" target=\"_blank\">Introduction Ancient Egypt and Its Civilisation</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.coursera.org/learn/magic-middle-ages\" target=\"_blank\">Magic in the Middle Ages</a></li> </ul></li> <li><i><i>Dark Eras 2</i></i><ul><li><i>TBA</i></li> </ul></li> <li><i>Mage Noir (<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/89457/Mage-Noir?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a>)</i><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.thegreatcoursesplus.com/history-of-the-united-states\" target=\"_blank\">History of the United States 2nd Edition</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://www.thegreatcoursesplus.com/the-us-and-the-middle-east-1914-to-9-11\" target=\"_blank\">The United States and the Midd